\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 27\nL0@P0: QF 09\nL1@P0: Media Preparation Recipe Template\nL2@P0: Revision: 002\nL3@P0: Approved: 29 MAY 26\nL4@P0: Created on:\nL5@P0: 29 May 2026\nL6@P0: CCAP (Culture Collection of Algae and Protozoa), SAMS Ltd,\nL7@P0: Scottish Association for Marine Science, Oban, Argyll, PA37 1QA\nL8@P0: Tel: +44 (0)1631 559000 Email: ccap@sams.ac.uk\nL9@P0: Web: www.ccap.ac.uk\nL10@P0: Page 1 of 1\nL11@P0: NCL75S (New Cereal Leaf-75% Seawater)\nL12@P0: Marine protozoa\nL13@P0: Medium per litre\nL14@P0: Natural filtered seawater 750.0 ml\nL15@P0: Deionised water 250.0 ml\nL16@P0: Cereal grass leaves* 1.0 g\nL17@P0: Bring 500 ml of 75% seawater to the boil then add cereal leaves. Continue to boil for 5 minutes.\nL18@P0: Allow to cool to room temperature and restore volume to 500 ml with deionised water. Filter\nL19@P0: through GF/C paper and then decant into the remaining 500 ml. Autoclave at 15 psi for 15\nL20@P0: minutes.\nL21@P0: Supply\nL22@P0: *Ward's Natural Science, PO Box 92912, Rochester, NY 14692-9012, USA, www.wardsci.com\nL23@P0: Reference\nL24@P0: D.M. Prescott; T.W. James (1955). Culturing of Amoeba proteus on Tetrahymena.\nL25@P0: Experimental Cell Research 8(1), 256–258. – adapted for CCAP\nL26@P0: Reviewed: 30th June 2026\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMedium data (https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=906)\nciteturn12view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=906\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 28\nL0: # Medium data\nL1: \nL2: Search for medium no. = [906].\nL3: \nL4: * * *\nL5: \nL6: Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121°C for 15 min.\nL7: \nL8: * * *\nL9: \nL10: 906   MK MEDIUM\nL11: Trisodium citrate·2H_{2}O  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL12: Tryptone (BD-Difco)  | ` 2.0    `  | g\nL13: Peptone (Oxoid)  | ` 1.0    `  | g\nL14: KH_{2}PO_{4}  | ` 0.6    `  | g\nL15: NH_{4}Cl  | ` 0.6    `  | g\nL16: NaCl  | ` 200.0    `  | g\nL17: MgCl_{2}·6H_{2}O  | ` 0.2    `  | g\nL18: K_{2}SO_{4}  | ` 20.0    `  | g\nL19: FeCl_{2}·4H_{2}O  | ` 36.0    `  | mg\nL20: MnCl_{2}·4H_{2}O  | ` 0.36   `  | mg\nL21: SL-6 trace element solution (see Medium No. 【0†167】)  | ` 1.0    `  | ml\nL22: Add components to distilled water and bring volume to 900 ml. Adjust pH to 7.0 and autoclave. For preparation of solid medium, add 20.0 g/L Bacto agar (BD-Difco). Separately autoclave the following solution:\nL23: 0.5 M Glycine-NaOH buffer (pH 10.0)  | ` 100.0    `  | ml\nL24: After autoclaving, add the solution to the medium.\nL25: * * *\nL26: \nL27: Copyright © 2026 Microbe Division (JCM) - All Rights Reserved\n"}
